        skos:definition        "An equation used to estimate the carbon content of transparent exopolymer particles (TEP) based on the equivalent spherical diameter of the particle and a fractal dimension value of 2.55. TEP-Carbon (ug) for each particle=0.25 x 10^-6 r^2.55. Mari, X. (1999). Carbon content and C:N ratio of transparent exopolymeric particles (TEP) produced by bubbling exudates of diatoms. Mar Ecol Prog Ser 183:59-71."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:S05::S050270";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "computation using Mari (1999) formula"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P01/current/TEPCSMP1/> .

